## Structural Map

Key files Claude reads first:
- `Program.cs` — host, DI registrations, middleware pipeline
- `Controllers/` or `Endpoints/` — HTTP surface; thin, delegate to services
- `Services/` — business logic and orchestration
- `Data/` — `DbContext`, entity configurations, migrations
- `Contracts/` or `Dtos/` — request/response shapes, validated at the boundary
- `tests/` — xUnit/NUnit projects; integration tests against a real database

Layers and their purpose:
- `Controllers/` → Bind and validate, call a service, map results to responses
- `Services/` → Business logic; no `DbContext` queries in controllers
- `Data/` → All persistence; migrations reviewed as SQL
- `tests/` → Real-persistence-path tests for P1/P2 (see `csharp-patterns.md`)

